-- CAPABILITY --------- errors/cap_grant_exceeded_3.march

`main` is granted `Cap(IO.Console)`, but the program reaches `IO.FileWrite` here. The grant is a ceiling on the WHOLE program — declaring `needs IO.FileWrite` does not raise it. [cap_grant_exceeded]
help: add a `Cap(IO.FileWrite)` parameter to `main` (e.g. `fn main(…, _cap_filewrite : Cap(IO.FileWrite))`), or widen the whole grant to `Cap(IO)`, or remove the use.

6 |     let _ = file_write("/tmp/count", int_to_string(n))
                ^^^^^^^^^^


    `main` calls `save` here:

11 |     save(1)
         ^^^^

    `main` is granted only `Cap(IO.Console)` here:

10 |   fn main(_c : Cap(IO.Console)) do
       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

    fix (`forge fix` applies it):

10 -   fn main(_c : Cap(IO.Console)) do
10 +   fn main(_c : Cap(IO.Console), _cap_filewrite : Cap(IO.FileWrite)) do

    run `march --explain cap_grant_exceeded`



